  "notes": "Carried with an explicit Gate 1 caveat — \"beat-scene rather than chart, included for his placements on charting alt-R&B albums\" — and the entry states the modelling parameter as a relationship rather than a value: \"**the parameter is the disagreement between layers** — a swung, off-grid kick and clap that do not line up with the quantised hats, plus crushed and bit-reduced drum timbres, snare timbre changes used as accents, and frequent half-time/double-time feel switches\". Two layers disagreeing is the loosest kick/snare jitter in the producer bench against a tight hat lane, a large `snare.offGridMs`, and a swing at the heavy end of the legal band. ⛔ **`bass808` is null**: \"a fat filtered sub with a fast decay, syncopated against the kick in 16ths — a funk bass line played by a synth rather than a sustained 808\", so the bass is `independent_riff` with high anticipation. Harmony is where he differs from the rest of the beat-scene bench, and the entry marks it: \"**more chord movement than the lane norm** — chopped jazz/soul fragments reharmonised across a 4-bar loop, plus bright major-key synth writing\", so a major family carries real weight and `maxChords` is 6. \"His beds are busier and higher-energy than the lane's whisper norm\" is the melody density and the bright `timbreHint`. ⚠ `confidence` is **low**, mirroring the entry's medium-low: \"his collective affiliations and placements are sourced; parametric detail is inference from the records\". ⚠ Every number here is **INFERRED**. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research. ⚠ **`drums.kick.lockTo808` removed (2026-08-17, 808 gate).** This kit has no 808 — `bass808` is `null` here or in the parent it inherits — and `lockTo808` is the one parameter that says *how much of the kick the 808 follows*, so in this file it described a pairing that does not exist: `generators::drums::bass808` returns on `block.is_none()` before the value is ever read, which makes it provably dead here. Where it was NOT dead was in the artists and producers who extend this kit and author an 808 of their own: they inherited the zero, `kicks.iter().filter(|_| rng.random_bool(0.0))` kept nothing, and their sub lane was silent at every seed — `bass808::every_shipped_model_with_an_808_produces_a_playable_line` reported \"no 808 at all\" for 35 of them. Removing it restores the engine's documented default of 1.0 for exactly those children and changes nothing here. ⚠ No researched claim moved: this kit's own statement about the 808 is the `bass808: null` beside it, and that is untouched.",
